Z||000000||GT GT 87||10-22-2001||07:54 PM||||I'm looking for roller rockers for my 3.2. Jegs has Comp Cam roller rockers (1.52/1) for 120$. GM Performance has GM roller rockers for late model V-6 , for 120$ , Part # 24504436. Will this work on my engine ? What is the ratio ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||10-22-2001||08:44 PM||||A GM technician has told me that the late model GM roller rockers will work but I can't say for sure he is right. I went with the Crane Gold Race Rockers. The Comp Cams roller tipped Magnum rocker arms are an excellent choice and I would go with them. The Comp Cams rocker arms will have more accurate ratios than the GM ones. The GM rocker arms are probably a 1.5 ratio rocker arm. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||watts||10-22-2001||11:33 PM||||I've got the 1.6:1 Comp Cams magnum roller tips on mine.<P>For some great prices (no, I don't work for them!) check out <A HREF="http://www.hi-performance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.hi-performance.com</A>  -- Remember that it's all in Canadian dollars, so it's like getting an instant %50 discount on everything for you folks down in the states!  I've bought the bulk of my engine parts from these guys.  Very friendly and helpful.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||10-23-2001||12:48 AM||||The late model GM are probably the pedistal mount rockers like on my 3400.||||reg||1
